    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8650" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cloelĭus</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clŭĭlĭus</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cloelĭa</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a Roman</i>
			gens: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">C. Cluilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 22, 4 al.</span></i>
			—Esp.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cloelĭa</span></b> , ae, f.,
				<i>a Roman maiden</i>, <i>who</i>,
				<i>when a hostage to Porsenna</i>, <i>with several companions</i>, <i>swam back to
			Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2, 13, 6</span></i> and 7; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8,
				651</span></i>; Piso ap. <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 6, 13, § 29
		al.</span></i></div>
